{"name":"Penzance","hex":"#627e75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Penzance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A coastal town, port, and civil parish with a town council in Cornwall, England .","A special service area in the Regional Municipality of Sarnia, No. 221, Saskatchewan, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Penzance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Penzance","blocks":[{"text":"Penzance is a town, civil parish and port in Cornwall, England. It lies 64 miles (103 km) west-southwest of Plymouth, 255 miles (410 km) west-southwest of London, and 9 miles (14 km) east of Land's End. Penzance railway station is the terminus of the Cornish Main Line and is both the southernmost and westernmost station in England. Situated in the shelter of Mount's Bay, the town faces south-east onto the English Channel. As well as Penzance itself, the parish also includes the fishing port of Newlyn and the villages of Mousehole, Paul, Gulval, and Heamoor. At the 2021 census the population of the parish was 20,734 and the population of the Penzance built-up area as defined by the Office for National Statistics was 14,960."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/PZHARBOURPANORAMA.jpg/330px-PZHARBOURPANORAMA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penzance","wikidata":"Q208209"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Penzance_Harbour_with_Scillonian_3_by_Kernow_Skies.jpg/500px-Penzance_Harbour_with_Scillonian_3_by_Kernow_Skies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Penzance_Harbour_with_Scillonian_3_by_Kernow_Skies.jpg/1280px-Penzance_Harbour_with_Scillonian_3_by_Kernow_Skies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com